{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1337876-self-made-deviant-running-their-own-conspiracy","id":1337876,"title":"Self-Made Deviant Running Their Own Conspiracy?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Deviant: The Renegades"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-25T16:49:34-07:00","id":1337876,"title":"Self-Made Deviant Running Their Own Conspiracy?","content":"So I was thinking about different ideas for Deviant characters, and I came up with one that I'm not sure would even work but raises some interesting questions.<br /> <br /> The character was a mortal psychic that was driven by a desire for power and wealth who used their powers to get very rich and build themselves an occult research organization to help develop ways to further enhance their powers. They used their powers to ensure loyalty; anyone who even thought too many traitorous thoughts had an unfortunate accident. But the truly loyal (not just opportunistic sycophants) were richly rewarded. Finally, there was a breakthrough, and when they tested it, it worked, but there were side effects, terrible side effects.<br /> <br /> So basically I was thinking that the character would be a Self-Made Autourgic Cephalist with 5 Dots each in Status(Occult Research Conspiracy) and Resources who funds and runs their own Conspiracy.<br /> <br /> So the questions I was wondering about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> Would this character be a Devoted? - I can see arguments for either way. Yes, because they are part of the Conspiracy and agree with its goals. No - because the Conspiracy works for the character and its goals are obeying the character and collecting more occult secrets and resources for the character.<br /> <br /> Does this violate some rule somewhere? - I'm not sure if this violates the rules for Conspiracies. I backed the Kickstarter but I didn't see rules for Conspiracies in either preview. Did I miss those (I tend to skip around reading things in order of what seems the most interesting) or are they coming later?<br /> <br /> EDIT: This kind of concept might even work for an entire cohort. Instead of just a single character, it could be a group acting as a board of directors for the Conspiracy and providing even greater benefits. All of them with Status 5 each but providing something different with the rest of their Merit dots. One with Resources 5, another with Safe Place 5, another with Staff 5, etc.<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: As for what they could be doing during the chronicle, they could be following the Web of Pain dismantling other Conspiracies and stealing their secrets and resources, and possibly punishing those who experiment on unwilling people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 09-25-2019, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T17:03:16-07:00","id":1337880,"title":"","content":"Per the Introduction, the Conspiracy rules are in Chapter Five, which spacing-wise suggests we've got another two weeks before we see them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T16:25:24-07:00","id":1340863,"title":"","content":"So it's been two weeks and we now have the Conspiracy mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1337876-self-made-deviant-running-their-own-conspiracy#post1337876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The character was a mortal psychic that was driven by a desire for power and wealth who used their powers to get very rich and build themselves an occult research organization to help develop ways to further enhance their powers. They used their powers to ensure loyalty; anyone who even thought too many traitorous thoughts had an unfortunate accident. But the truly loyal (not just opportunistic sycophants) were richly rewarded. Finally, there was a breakthrough, and when they tested it, it worked, but there were side effects, terrible side effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the big problem: You're leaning on unspecified pre-Divergence psychic powers that far outstrip the limits of available Variations for this setup. The character no longer has that degree or type of power, and to the extent that they can manage it at all now, it's starkly metered by (as a Cephalist) their ability to spend Willpower; they inherently cannot keep watch over every member of their conspiracy, which means they have to delegate and let the problems that &quot;benign&quot; conspiracies deal with creep in where they aren't looking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would this character be a Devoted? - I can see arguments for either way. Yes, because they are part of the Conspiracy and agree with its goals. No - because the Conspiracy works for the character and its goals are obeying the character and collecting more occult secrets and resources for the character. </div> </div> </div>Unless they grow and are driven primarily by hatred and vengeance, this is a Devoted. As mentioned above, unless they spend an impossible amount of their time micromanaging their conspiracy, its goals cannot actually be &quot;obeying the character&quot; as a matter of policy, particularly not if it's going to survive the blowback of picking fights with other conspiracies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}